---
description: Lando Design System project conventions — read AGENTS.md before writing code
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` in the project root before writing code. It is the single brief
for this project; this rule only points at it.

The essentials, so you don't need to open it for small edits:

- Built on `@lando-labs/lando-ds`. **Use the design system — don't rebuild it.**
  A `lando-ds` MCP server is configured (`.cursor/mcp.json`); ask it for
  components, props, and tokens rather than assuming an API from memory.
- **No Tailwind or utility CSS.** Style only via DS components and design tokens.
  A hardcoded hex, spacing, or font size is a bug.
- **Server Components by default**; `'use client'` only for interactivity.
- **The theme preset lives in `app/providers.tsx`** — read it before any color
  decision. Changing it takes two matching edits (`providers.tsx` and the
  `themeScript({ defaultPreset })` call in `app/layout.tsx`), or the app flashes
  the wrong palette on load.
- **Never add an unlayered global reset** — the app reset belongs in
  `@layer app-reset`. Deliberate overrides go in `@layer app`.

Anything beyond this: open `AGENTS.md`.
